@startuml
title OneDrive Client for Linux - Authentication Paths

participant "OneDrive Client\nfor Linux" as Client
participant "Local OAuth\nloopback listener" as LocalAuth
participant "Web Browser / User" as Browser
participant "Microsoft Identity\nplatform" as Identity
participant "Intune / broker\nwhen configured" as Intune
participant "Microsoft Graph API" as Graph

alt Intune broker authentication is configured
  Client -> Intune: Attempt silent token acquisition from cached account state
  alt Silent acquisition succeeds
    Intune --> Client: Access token + expiry/account data
  else Silent acquisition fails / no cached account
    Client -> Intune: Start interactive broker authentication
    Intune -> Identity: Microsoft identity / Conditional Access flow
    Identity --> Intune: Authentication result
    Intune --> Client: Access token + expiry/account data
  end
else Standard OAuth authentication
  alt Valid refresh token is available
    Client -> Identity: Refresh-token grant over HTTPS
    Identity --> Client: Access token + refresh token / expiry
  else Device authorisation is configured
    Client -> Identity: Request device code
    Identity --> Client: Verification URI + user code + polling interval
    Client -> Browser: Ask user to visit verification URI and enter code
    Browser -> Identity: User authentication / consent / MFA if required
    loop Until authorised, declined or expired
      Client -> Identity: Poll device-code token endpoint
      Identity --> Client: Pending / error / token response
    end
  else Interactive authorisation code flow
    alt Local browser callback is available
      Client -> LocalAuth: Bind available loopback port
      Client -> Browser: Open Microsoft authorisation URL
      Browser -> Identity: User authentication / consent / MFA if required
      Identity --> Browser: Redirect to loopback URI with code
      Browser -> LocalAuth: GET callback URI
      LocalAuth --> Client: Authorisation code
      Client -> Identity: Redeem code at token endpoint
      Identity --> Client: Access token + refresh token / expiry
      LocalAuth --> Browser: Authentication completion response
    else Manual redirect URI workflow
      Client -> Browser: Display authorisation URL
      Browser -> Identity: User authentication / consent / MFA if required
      Identity --> Browser: Redirect URI containing code
      Browser --> Client: User pastes full redirect URI
      Client -> Client: Extract authorisation code
      Client -> Identity: Redeem code at token endpoint
      Identity --> Client: Access token + refresh token / expiry
    end
  end
end

== Authenticated API operation ==
Client -> Graph: Microsoft Graph request with bearer access token
Graph --> Client: API response

opt Access token expires during runtime
  Client -> Identity: Refresh-token grant or applicable broker renewal
  Identity --> Client: New access token / expiry
end
@enduml
